 investors which are due 2018 raising cash of $37.2m net of issue costs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bonds have an annual coupon of 8 per cent per annum payable semi-annually in arrears. The Bonds are convertible into ordinary shares of the Company at any time from 1 April 2013 up until seven days prior to their maturity on 19 February 2018 at a conversion price of 76.29 pence per Ordinary Share, unless the Company settles the conversion notice by paying the Bondholder the Cash Alternative Amount (see below).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Interest, after the deduction of issue costs and the inclusion of the redemption premium, will be charged to the income statement using an effective rate of 18.0%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cash Alternative Amount\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At the option of the Company, the conversion notice in respect of the Bonds can be settled in cash rather than shares, the Cash Alternative Amount payable is based on the Volume Weighted Average Price of the Company's shares prior to the conversion notice.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Credit Facility\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On 31 March 2011, Poltava Petroleum Company ('PPC'), our subsidiary in Ukraine, entered into a reducing credit facility agreement with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cr\u233\'00\'E9dit Agricole\f28 \uc2 \f2  CIB (France) secured by indemnity provided by the parent company, \f28 \uc2 \f2 JKX Oil & Gas plc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The credit facility was for a maximum of the Ukrainian Hryvnia equivalent of $15.0m and expired on 30 June 2015; discussions are currently underway to renew this facility. All provisions contained in the credit facility documentation were negotiated on normal commercial and customary terms for such finance arrangements. The interest was calculated at prevailing \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cr\u233\'00\'E9dit Agricole\f28 \uc2 \f2  CIB (France) bank rate plus a margin.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    10.   Derivatives \par  \par                                                   30 June   30 June   31 December \par  