ivables and the maximum credit risk exposure.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The maximum financial exposure due to credit risk on the Group's financial assets, representing the sum of cash and cash equivalents, trade receivables, held to maturity financial investments and other current assets, as at 30 June 2015 was $26.1m (31 December 2014: $32.8m).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Capital management - Group\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Directors determine the appropriate capital structure of the Group specifically, how much is raised from shareholders (equity) and how much is borrowed from financial institutions (debt) in order to finance the Group's business strategy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group's policy as to the level of equity capital and reserves is to ensure that it maintains a strong financial position and low gearing ratio which provides financial flexibility to continue as a going concern and to maximise shareholder value. The capital structure of the Group consists of shareholders' equity together with net debt. The Group's funding requirements are met through a combination of debt, equity and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cash flow.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Net debt\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Net debt comprises: borrowings disclosed in note 9 and total cash in note 7, and excludes derivatives. Equity attributable to the shareholders of the Company comprises issued capital, capital reserves and retained earnings, (see Condensed consolidated statement of changes in equity).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The capital structure of the Group is as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                                                   30 June   31 December \par                                                                      2015          2014 \par                                                                      $000          $000 \par ----------------------------------------------------  -------------------  -----------