\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-UPDATE 2-\uc2 Ukraine's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  buys $62 mln to steady confused hryvnia market\b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2015\par 19:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Changes transliteration of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head's surname to Gontareva in final paragraph)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Feb 27 (Reuters) - \uc2 Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $62.35 million at a rate of 27.5 hryvnias to the dollar on the interbank market on Friday, its third \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week to limit volatility for the struggling national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the bank sold dollars at a rate of 28.046, the same price it had paid for them the previous day, action that appeared to help stabilise the hryvnia, which has lost nearly half its value since the start of February.\par \par \uc2 "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to do this (buying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when there is a lack of buyers and selling when demand rises) then they should be able to keep the hryvnia steady," said a trader at a large bank in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 , speaking on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are aimed at ironing out imbalances in the market as a result of strict rules for exporters and importers on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales and purchases.\par \par \uc2 Trades registered on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's website took place on Friday at an average rate of 28.45 as of 1330 GMT, boosting the hryvnia 5 percent from the opening.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightened \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules for importers on Monday, a move that traders said was holding up deals, resulting in a lack of buyers on the market for the dollars that exporters are required to sell.\par \par \uc2 "A panic mood prevails in the market, therefore, in order to stop the frenzy, the bank is introducing additional administrative measures," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief \uc2 Valeria Gontareva\uc2  told a meeting of business leaders in Kiev. (Reporting by Natalia Zinets; Writing by Alessandra Prentice; Editing by Kevin Liffey) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-2-27T19:36:11.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150227eb2r00dvb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
