\par\par \b \uc2 Ukraine  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says has spent over $300 mln in indirect  \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions \highlight\uc2  in Feb.\b0\par\par\uc2 107 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 2015\par 14:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Feb 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold more than $300 million to state energy importers since the start of February in indirect \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the struggling hryvnia, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Valeriia Gontareva said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not left the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, casting it adrift ... the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  every day, but these \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are only on critical energy resources," she said in parliament.\par \par \uc2 The sales were mostly to state energy firm Naftogaz.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Natalia Zinets; Writing by Alessandra Prentice)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-2-21T13:41:07.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150218eb2i00kra\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
