\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  hryvnia crashes 12 pct as Kiev ends  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chris Vellacott \par \uc2 497 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2015\par 11:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hryvnia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped 12 percent to a record low against the dollar on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would stop using dollars to defend it, hiking rates instead.\par \par \uc2 The hryvnia fell to 18.75 to the dollar and Ukraine's dollar bond spread against U.S. Treasuries widened 13 basis points to 2941 bps.\par \par \uc2 With \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves dwindling, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Valeriia Gontareva said there would be no more market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rates will rise 550 basis points to 19.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Reserves stood at $7.5 billion by end-2014, enough to fund five weeks of imports.\par \par \uc2 "They can't afford to lose more \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves but I don't think higher interest rates will scare people away from selling the Ukrainian hryvnia. It's more about economic failings and the war situation at this stage," said Simon Quijano Evans head of emerging market research at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 Quijano-Evans said as long as conflict continued to rage in eastern Ukraine, international lenders would be reluctant to top up reserves with aid.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian dollar debt fell across the board, with a $1.25 billion bond maturing in 2023 down 0.85 cents to trade at 50.5 cents in the dollar, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets were pressured by oil's retreat and a cut in the ratings of some of the country's top companies by \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  . Energy firms Rosneft and \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  were cut to non-investment grade.\par \par \uc2 The rouble slipped 0.3 percent while Moscow's dollar-denominated RTS index fell 0.4 percent.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's lira climbed 0.6 percent against the dollar, recovering from a record low hit a day earlier after President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  made fresh criticism of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies, stoking worries over the bank's independence.\par \par \uc2 Broader emerging stocks were lower with the MSCI emerging equities index retreating 0.4 percent following a weak session in China as a cut in the reserve requirement ratio failed to impress investors.\par \par \uc2 The Shanghai index dropped 1.2 percent.\par \par \uc2 In central Europe, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased after the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cancelled its acceptance of Greek bonds in return for funding.\par \par \uc2 The Czech crown was 0.1 percent weaker, Hungary's forint fell 0.4 percent while the Polish zloty was flat.\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  performance 2015, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jus35t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jus35t }}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging index performance 2015, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/weh36s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/weh36s }}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging Europe performance 2015, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jun28s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jun28s }}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHI