ghlight\uc2 \f2  are of a continuing nature.\par \par This financial information has been prepared under the historical cost\par convention, as modified by the revaluation of investments and derivative\par financial instruments at fair value through profit or loss.\par \par (b) Valuation of investments\par \par Upon initial recognition the investments are designated by the Company as "at\par fair value through profit or loss". They are included initially at fair value\par which is taken to be their cost, including expenses incidental to purchase.\par Subsequently the investments are valued at fair value which is bid market price\par for listed investments. Unquoted investments are included at a valuation\par determined by the Directors after discussion with the Alternative Investment\par Fund Manager on the basis of the latest accounting and other relevant\par information.\par \par Changes in the fair value of investments held at fair value through profit or\par loss and gains or losses on disposal are included in the capital column of the\par income statement within "Gains/(losses) from investments held at fair value\par through profit or loss". All purchases and sales are accounted for on a trade\par date basis.\par \par Year-end exchange rates are used to translate the value of investments which\par are denominated in foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \par (c) Foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par \par Transactions denominated in foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are translated into sterling at\par actual exchange rates as at the date of the transaction or, where appropriate,\par at the rate of exchange in a related forward exchange contract. Monetary assets\par and liabilities denominated in foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the year-end are reported\par at the rates of exchange prevailing at the year-end or, where appropriate, at\par the rate of exchange in a related forward exchange contract. Any gain or loss\par arising from a change in exchange rates subsequent to the date of the\par transaction is included as an exchange gain or loss in capital reserve. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements on fixed asset investments are included in the Income\par Statement within gains on investments held at fair value through profit or\par loss.\par \par (d) Income\par \par Investment income, which includes related taxation, has been accounted for on\par an ex-dividend basis or when the Company's right to the income is established.\par \par Interest receivable on deposits is accounted for on an accruals basis.\par \par (e) Expenses\par \par All expenses are accounted for on an accruals basis and are charged as follows:\par \par the basic investment management fee is charged 50% to revenue and 50% to\par capital from 1 October 2013 (prior to this it was charged 100% to revenue);\par \par any investment performance bonus payable to Baring Fund Managers Limited is\par charged wholly to capital;\par \par dealing costs are charged wholly to capital; and\par \par other expenses are charged wholly to revenue.\par \par (f) Interest payable\par \par Interest payable is accounted for on an accruals basis, and is charged wholly\par to revenue.\par \par (g) Capital reserve\par \par Gains or losses on disposal of investments and changes in fair values of\par investments are transferred to the capital reserve. Any investment performance\par fee payable to Baring Fund Managers Limited is accounted for in the capital\par reserve.\par \par (h) Special reserve\par \par Pursuant to a special resolution passed on 8 November 2002, the Company's\par application to reduce its share premium account was approved by the High Court\par and registered with the Registrar of Companies on 18 December 2002. The amount\par of the reduction was \u163\'00\'A386,624,982, representing the share premium arising on the\par issue of shares by the Company on 17 December 2002. This amount was transferred\par to a special reserve which has been utilised for the repurchase by the Company\par of its own shares.\par \par (i) Taxation\par \par The charge for taxation is based upon the net revenue for the year. The tax\par charge is allocated to the revenue and capital accounts according to the\par marginal basis whereby revenue expenses are first matched against taxable\par income arising in the revenue account; the effect of this for the year ended 30\par September 2014 was that all the deductions for tax purposes went to the revenue\par account.\par \par Deferred taxation will be recognised as an asset or a liability if transactions\par have occurred at the balance sheet date that give rise to an obligation to pay\par more taxation in the future, or a right to pay less taxation in the future. An\par asset will not be recognised to the extent that the transfer of economic\par benefit is uncertain.\par \par 2. Income\par \par                                                 2014                      2013\par \par                                                 \u163\'00\'A3000                      \u163\'00\'A3000\par \par Income from investments\par \par Overseas dividends -                           5,903                     7,490\par Quoted\par \par                                                5,903                     7,490\par \par 3. Investment management fee\par \par Baring Fund Managers Limited ("BFM") acts as the Alternative Investment Fund\par Manager ("AIFM") of the Company under an agreement terminable by either party\par giving not less than six months' written notice. Under this agreement BFM\par receives a basic fee (charged 50% to revenue and 50% to capital) which is\par calculated monthly and payable at an annual rate of 0.8% of the net asset value\par of the Company. From 1 October 2013 the Directors decided upon a policy of\par allocating the investment management fees charging 50% to the revenue account\par and 50% to the capital account.\par \par In addition under the agreement BFM is entitled to a performance fee (charged\par to capital) which is payable at the rate of 10% of the amount by which the\par change in the Company's net asset value per share (on a total return basis)\par exceeds the Benchmark Index and any previous underperformance must be recovered\par before any fee is payable. The performance fee is capped at 0.6% of the net\par asset value of the Company on the first day of the performance period. The\par performance fee is calculated annually on 30 September. The whole of the\par performance fee is charged to the capital account as it is deemed to have\par arisen entirely as a result of the capital performance of the Company. No\par performance fee was payable for either of the years ended 30 September 2014 and\par 30 September 2013.\par \par The investment management fee comprises:\par \par                                                 2014                      2013\par \par                                                 \u163\'00\'A3000                      \u163\'00\'A3000\par \par Basic fee (50% charged to                        594                     1,439\par revenue from 1 October\par 2013; prior to this 100%\par was charged to revenue)\par \par Basic fee (50% charged to                        592                         -\par capital from 1 October\par 2013)\par \par                                                1,186                     1,439\par \par At 30 September 2014, \u163\'00\'A3188,000 (30 September 2013: \u163\'00\'A3216,000) of this fee\par remained outstanding.\par \par 4. Other expenses\par \par                                                  2014                      2013\par \par                                                  \u163\'00\'A3000                      \u163\'00\'A3000\par \par Custody and administrat