\par\par \b \uc2 Rouble falls back to  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  level as oil and  \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  weigh\b0\par\par\uc2 585 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2014\par 09:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 The Russian rouble weakened on Friday morning, again hitting the level where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  automatically defends it, as markets fretted over falling oil prices and continued fighting in eastern Ukraine despite a month-old ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 At 0710 GMT the rouble was 0.48 percent weaker against the dollar at 39.76 and lost 0.38 percent to at 50.23 versus the euro. This has left the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  0.4 percent weaker at 44.48 against the dollar-euro basket monitored by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  automatically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the rouble weakens beyond 44.40 against the basket, the edge of the rouble's corridor. The rouble first breached this level on Oct. 1, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rouble since May.\par \par \uc2 During trading hours on Thursday the rouble was stable despite a steep decline in the price of oil, Russia's main export. However, the rouble fell towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level in after-hours trading and again reached that level on Friday's market opening.\par \par \uc2 The rouble fell despite a partial recovery in the oil price. Brent, which touched $92 on Thursday, was trading at around $93.75 on Friday morning.\par \par \uc2 The rouble had been supported on Thursday by a general weakening of the dollar, but the dollar was again strengthening against global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Trading volumes were light on Thursday, but more significant volumes on Friday meant that a shift in the corridor was likely, said Mikhail Palei, head of conversion \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at VTB Capital.\par \par \uc2 "Judging by the quotations and the volume of deals on the exchange ($1.4 billion), the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could raise the corridor to 35.45 to 44.45," he said.\par \par \uc2 Once the bank has spent $350 million on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  it automatically moves the rouble's trading corridor by 5 kopecks. As of Thursday the corridor stretched from 35.40 to 44.40.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor \uc2 Elvira Nabiullina\uc2  said on Thursday that the bank has made just over $4 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Oct. 1 - a small amount compared with the amount needed to move the corridor, but the first time the bank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since May 7.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes were mixed, with the losses concentrated in the dollar-denominated RTS index that is dragged down by the weakening rouble.\par \par \uc2 At 0710 GMT the RTS was down 0.35 percent to 1,091 points, while the rouble-based MICEX was 0.04 percent higher at 1,377 points.\par \par \uc2 This follows steep declines on Thursday linked to the falling oil price, as well as a resumption of fighting in eastern Ukraine, where separatist rebels are attacking government forces holding the airport of the regional capital Donetsk.\par \par \uc2 "There are no grounds for optimism," BCS analyst Mark Bradford said in a morning note\par \par \uc2 He added that the Russian market was under pressure because of geopolitical tensions in Ukraine and Syria, as well as expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve will continue to wind down its monetary stimulus.\par \par \uc2 "The uncertainty over the lifting of sanctions (over Ukraine) has been transformed into worry about the threat of introducing new measures if the separatists continue the offensive in eastern Ukraine," he wrote.\par \par \uc2 For rouble poll data see\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see\par \par \uc2 Russia in graphics: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/dun63s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/dun63s}}}\uc2  (Reporting By Jason Bush and Vladimir Abramov) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-3T08:40:32.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141003eaa30086i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
