\par\par \b \uc2 NORDIC MORNING BRIEFING: PMI Figures In Focus\b0\par\par\uc2 By Christina Zander   \par \uc2 3,979 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 2014\par 05:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR - All times GMT \par Nordic Macro \par  \par 0630 Sweden, PMI \par 0700 Norway, PMI \par 0900 Denmark,PMI \par  \par Other Macro \par  \par 0100 China, Manufacturing PMI \par 0145 China, HSBC Industrial PMI, Aug. \par 0600 Germany, GDP, 2Q \par 0800 EMU, Industrial PMI, Aug. \par 0900 Greece, GDP, 2Q \par  \par IN FOCUS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The local focus Monday will be on PMI data from Sweden, Norway and Denmark. The data follow Friday's surprisingly weak GDP data from Denmark, which showed that economic output fell in the second quarter, disappointing analysts who had expected the economy to grow.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The second quarter fall reflects a weak trend in industrial production and mining, as well as slack demand for exports, the statistics agency said.\par \par \uc2 Globally Monday, there's a steady stream of PMI data from both Europe and China as well as Germany's GDP figure for the second quarter.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, investors will turn their attention to rate decisions from Sweden's Riksbank as well as from the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The local focus will also be on Finland's GDP figures for the second quarter. Finland slipped into a recession in the first quarter and the country has warned that its already struggling economy could be pushed toward disaster as Western sanctions against Russia, the Nordic country's third biggest export market, begin to have an effect.\par \par \uc2 U.S President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  will visit the Baltics on Tuesday to Thursday. He will travel to Estonia to discuss "collective defense" with the Baltic states, as the White House looks to reaffirm its commitment to defend \uc2 NATO\uc2  allies amid unrest in nearby Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Swedish industrial production figures for June will be in focus later on Friday, after the country's manufacturing production plummeted in May. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par  \par EUR/NOK \par Latest 0250 GMT 8.1319-96 \par Previous 2100 GMT 8.1304-88 \par %Chg +0.01 \par  \par EUR/SEK \par Latest 0250 GMT 9.1740-822 \par Previous 2100 GMT 9.1754-846 \par %Chg -0.02 \par  \par USD/NOK \par Latest 0250 GMT 6.1972-2020 \par Previous 2100 GMT 6.1934-88 \par %Chg  +0.06 \par  \par USD/SEK \par Latest 0250 GMT 6.9913-64 \par Previous 2100 GMT 6.9893-957 \par %Chg +0.02 \par  \par NORDIC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The main focus for the Nordics this week will be rate decisions by Sweden's Riksbank and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Riksbank is widely expected to leave its main interest rate unchanged after a surprisingly big 50-basis-point cut to 0.25% in June.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , is also expected to leave its key interest rate unchanged, but to launch a qualitative easing programme in the upcoming months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro-zone inflation data Friday showed price increases in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  block cooled to 0.3% on the year from 0.4% in July, in line with expectations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The news helped the euro touch a high for the day of $1.3195, even though disappointing German retail figures once again underscored the fragility of the region's recovery. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STOCK INDEXES: \par  \par OMXN40 1346.91   +6.37   +0.5% \par OMXS30 1388.89   +5.86   +0.4% \par OBX     556.88   -3.36   -0.6% \par OMXC20  737.12   -1.74   -0.2% \par OMXH25 2938.18  +16.80   +0.6% \par  \par Brent  $103.26   +0.07   +0.1% \par  \par NORDIC MARKETS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With a thin agenda, Nordic equity investors will this week focus on second-quarter earnings from Danish toy maker Lego, due Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Geopolitical tensions in Ukraine and Syria remain in focus, but a steady stream of global PMI and GDP data as well as the rate decision from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday are also potential market movers this week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nordic markets close mixed Friday as investors speculated whether lackluster euro-zone inflation data were weak enough to trigger more easing from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 Statoil\f28 \uc2 \f2  traded down 1.3% as the company's chief executive said more complex, risky projects have led to "escalating investments, increased cost and declining returns". \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ENERGY: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil futures were mixed in Asian trade, following negative Chinese manufacturing data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nymex crude was down 17 cents at $95.79/bbl. Brent crude was up 7 cents at $103.26/bbl.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Both Nymex and Brent, which fell 2.25% and 2.67%, respectively, in August, have been lower for two consecutive months but recovered slightly in the final week of August on the back of positive U.S. economic data and Russia-Ukraine tensions. Other U.S. data this week are likely to drive price direction in WTI with the potential for further gains in Brent as well, ANZ said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEWS ROUNDUP: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DENMARK: Denmark's economic output fell in the second three months of the year, hit by weak exports, disappointing analysts who had expected the economy to grow. Denmark's gross domestic product fell 0.3% on the quarter, the official statistics agency said Friday, after a 0.6% rise in the first quarter.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FINLAND: Finland's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rovio Entertainment Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., maker of the Angry Birds mobile game, said on Friday that Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mikael Hed\f28 \uc2 \f2  will step down in January--a move that comes amid the company's recent struggles to refresh its games lineup and revenue model. Mr. Hed will be replaced by former \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nokia Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 executive Pekka Rantala\f28 \uc2 \f2 , who joined Rovio's executive team earlier this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: The Chinese-backed company trying to revive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Saab\f28 \uc2 \f2  cars encountered a roadblock Friday as it lost the right to use the Swedish brand's name as it negotiates with potential investors on a plan to reconstruct the business.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bombardier Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s CSeries single-aisle jetliner program has suffered another setback as Swedish carrier Braathens Aviation said it would step back from its role as the first operator of the plane and that it may seek other changes to delivery plans.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Christina Zander at christina.zander@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1 Sep 2014 22:42 ET \par Nordic Morning Briefing: Geopolitics In Focus\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Sven Grundberg \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR - All times GMT \par Nordic Macro \par  \par 0730 Sweden Current Account, 2Q \par  \par Other Macro \par  \par 0900 Euro Zone PPI, July \par 1000 \f28 \uc2 \f2 OECD\f28 \uc2 \f2 CPI\f28 \uc2 \f2 , July \par 1345 US ISM New York, Aug. \par 1400 US Manufacturing ISM, Aug. \par 1500 Global Markit PMI Manufacturing, Aug. \par  \par IN FOCUS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Geopolitics are firmly in focus this week, as the stakes have been raised in Ukraine where the country's military has seen fortunes dramatically reversed on the battlefield in the nation's east.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ukraine, backed by Western leaders, attributes recent military setbacks to more than 1,000 troops that Moscow allegedly has sent into its territory in the last few weeks to support separatists.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Germany's Chancellor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Angela Merkel\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Monday stressed the need for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  to prepare more sanctions, citing Russia's "unacceptable" behavior in Ukraine. Russia and President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vladimir Putin\f28 \uc2 \f2 , on the other hand, have called on Kiev to agree to an immediate and unconditional cease-fire.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the Nordics, meanwhile, investors are looking ahead to Thursday's rate decision by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sweden's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Riksbank. Analysts polled by The Wall Street Journal said they expect the Riksbank to leave its main repo rate at 0.25%, but to leave the door open for lower rates if inflation fails to accelerate. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par  \par EUR/NOK \par Latest 0150 GMT 8.1211-96 \par Previous 2150 GMT 8.1244-335 \par %Chg -0.04 \par  \par EUR/SEK \par Latest 0150 GMT 9.1919-98 \par Previous 2150 GMT 9.1914-2017 \par %Chg -0.01 \par  \par USD/NOK \par Latest 0150 GMT 6.1898-954 \par Previous 2150 GMT 6.1889-947 \par %Chg +0.01 \par  \par USD/SEK \par Latest 0150 GMT 7.0059-110 \par Previous 2150 GMT 7.0016-81 \par %Chg +0.05 \par  \par NORDIC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Divergent PMI figures from Norway and Sweden on Monday sent the Norwegian krone strongly higher and the Swedish krona reeling. The NOK/SEK cross powered to a new 14-month high, but the move has breached a falling five-year downtrend resistance line at 1.1299.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Swedish PMI fell to 51.0 in August from 55.2 in July, highlighting that Sweden's economy, like much of Europe, remains in a slow and uneven recovery with domestic consumption just about offsetting muted demand for Swedish goods overseas.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In focus this week is the rate decision by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sweden's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday. Analysts polled by The Wall Street Journal said they expect the Riksbank to leave its main repo rate at 0.25% at the meeting, but to leave the door open for lower rates if inflation fails to accelerate during autumn.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts at SEB bank said they expect the Riksbank to say it now foresees a rate rise in the first quarter of 2016 compared with expectations in July for an increase in the fourth quarter of next year. The Riksbank's forecasts are likely to continue to signal a chance of easing later this year and SEB expects to see a rate cut to 0.15% in October.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sweden's industrial production data for July is due on Friday, and will be closely eyed after Monday's weak PMI data. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STOCK INDEXES: \par  \par OMXN40 1344.77   -2.14   -0.2% \par OMXS30 1386.97   -1.92   -0.1% \par OBX     560.81   +3.93   +0.7% \par OMXC20  737.73   +0.61   +0.1% \par OMXH25 2934.07   -4.11   -0.1% \par  \par Brent  $102.80   +0.01   +0.0% \par  \par NORDIC MARKETS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After suffering a sell-off late last week, which analysts attributed to geopolitical tensions, European markets continued to trade lower on Monday after Russia's foreign minister said Moscow will defend the economy if it comes up against another round of sanctions related to the conflict in Ukraine.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Saturday, EU leaders agreed to draw up options for new sanctions within a week if Russia doesn't pull back its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ukraine\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With a thin corporate agenda on Tuesday, the focus remains on the standoff between the West and Russia amid the ongoing conflict in Ukraine.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Trading volumes in European markets are set to return to more normal levels on Tuesday, after lighter than usual volumes on Monday with the close of trade in the U.S. for the Labor Day holiday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ENERGY: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil futures were steady in Asian trade, with Nymex crude down 11 cents at $95.85/bbl and Brent crude up 1 cent at $102.80/bbl.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil markets continue to sway between oversupply concerns and international tensions. U.S. and European officials are discussing new sanctions against Russia, while Libya's outgoing cabinet has acknowledged it lost control of capital Tripoli to Islamist militias.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Libyan crude oil output has recovered from the start of the year, averaging 500,000 bbl/day at the end of August, but remains well below its long-term average of 1.6 million bbl/day," ANZ said. Capital Economics noted a strong U.S. dollar has weighed on commodity prices, including oil. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEWS ROUNDUP: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN'S purchasing managers' index for manufacturers fell in August, causing investors to back away from the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as further easing from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  began to look more likely. The Swedish PMI fell to 51.0 in August from 55.2 in July.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: Tests results have shown that a man who was hospitalized in Sweden on Sunday as a suspected Ebola case isn't carrying the potentially deadly virus, Stockholm County Council health officials said in a news release on Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FINLAND: A nuclear reactor under construction in Finland is now estimated to start \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2018, nearly a decade later than originally planned. The French nuclear group Areva AS is building the reactor in consortium with Germany's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Siemens AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  for Finnish utility \f28 \uc2 \f2 Teollisuuden Voima Oyj\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or TVO. The plant has been under construction since 2005.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN'S government this weekend inked a letter of intent with the Czech Republic and Slovakia regarding the Swedish Gripen jet fighter, potentially opening the door for its introduction in one more Eastern European country. Gripen has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the Czech Republic since 2005.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Sven Grundberg at sven.grundberg@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @svengrundberg\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2 Sep 2014 22:24 ET \par Nordic Morning Briefing: Geopolitics in Focus\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Christina Zander \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR - All times GMT \par Nordic Macro \par  \par 0630 Sweden, PMI Services, Aug \par 0903 Sweden to sell 2020, \par       2025 bonds \par 1800 U.S Beige Book \par  \par Other Macro \par  \par 0900 Eurozone Aug Services PMI \par 0900 Eurozone, GDP, 2Q \par 0900 Eurozone July Retail Sales \par  \par IN FOCUS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Geopolitics remain in focus with the EU's Italian Foreign Minister Federica Mogherini--chosen on Saturday to be the bloc's next foreign policy chief, saying Tuesday the union should decide on a new round of sanctions against Russia "by Friday," and labelling Russia's actions in Ukraine "an aggression." She added, "I think that we need to respond in the strongest possible way to that."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Several diplomats said Tuesday the EU may restrict access to financial markets for Russian state-owned companies beyond the banking sector and is likely to expand the ban on exports of dual-use goods to Russia. If adopted, the new measures would modestly increase pressure on Russia over the Ukraine crisis but fall short of delivering a powerful blow to the Russian economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia ramped up its rhetoric Tuesday, calling on the U.S. to push Kiev into giving up its military campaign and negotiating a political deal. On Sunday, Mr. Putin called for talks on statehood for eastern Ukraine, although his spokesman later clarified that he meant more independence from Kiev.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Locally, the focus will be on U.S President Barak Obama's visit to Estonia to reassure the region, rattled by Russia's incursion into Ukraine, that \f28 \uc2 \f2 NATO\f28 \uc2 \f2  remains committed to defending its Baltic members.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Estonian President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toomas Hendrik Ilves\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday, ahead of the president's visit, that he wants a permanent presence of \f28 \uc2 \f2 North Atlantic Treaty Organization\f28 \uc2 \f2  troops in his country, and warned against a two-tier \f28 \uc2 \f2 NATO\f28 \uc2 \f2  in the face of potential aggressors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NATO\f28 \uc2 \f2  leaders are this week set to approve a military unit to be kept on permanent high alert that can move rapidly when a crisis arises, Secretary-General Anders Fogh Rasmussen said on Monday. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par  \par EUR/NOK \par Latest 0150 GMT 8.1271-356 \par Previous 2150 GMT 8.1219-301 \par %Chg +0.07 \par  \par EUR/SEK \par Latest 0150 GMT 9.2149-204 \par Previous 2150 GMT 9.2096-175 \par %Chg +0.04 \par  \par USD/NOK \par Latest 0150 GMT 6.1902-58 \par Previous 2150 GMT 6.1847-900 \par %Chg +0.09 \par  \par USD/SEK \par Latest 0150 GMT 7.0187-220 \par Previous 2150 GMT 7.0130-82 \par %Chg +0.07 \par  \par NORDIC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In focus in the Nordics this week is the rate decision by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sweden's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday. Analysts polled by The Wall Street Journal said they expect the Riksbank to leave its main repo rate at 0.25% at the meeting, but to leave the door open for lower rates if inflation fails to accelerate during autumn. The Riksbank cut its key interest rate by 50 basis points to 0.25% in July as inflation had undershot the target for a long time.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thursday also brings the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy meeting. In response to weak growth and very low inflation, ECB officials provided additional stimulus at their June meeting and said more would be available if the eurozone's economic prospects didn't improve.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 's statistics agency said Tuesday that producer prices fell 0.1% from June, and were down 1.1% from July 2014. Producer prices rose in June, but that is the only month this year in which they have done so.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That prices of goods leaving the eurozone's factory gates resumed their decline in July, is an indication that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  area won't soon escape a lengthening period of very low inflation that threatens to undermine its fragile economy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STOCK INDEXES: \par  \par OMXN40  1,346.98   +2.21  +0.2% \par OMXS30  1,387.94   +0.97  +0.1% \par OBX       562.43   +1.62  +0.3% \par OMXC20    738.21   +0.48  +0.1% \par OMXH25  2,952.07  +18.0   +0.6% \par  \par Brent    $100.57  +$0.23  +0.2% \par  \par NORDIC MARKETS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European stocks wavered between gains and losses Tuesday, with investors moving with caution as they wait for definitive word on whether the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will approve a new round of monetary stimulus.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 's statistics agency said Tuesday that producer prices fell 0.1% from June, and were down 1.1% on the year, an indication that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  area won't soon escape a lengthening period of very low inflation that threatens to undermine its fragile economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nordic markets closed the session higher Tuesday following better than expected U.S manufacturing data in the afternoon. The OMXN40 was up 0.2% at 1,346.98; Olso's OBX closed up 0.3% at 562.43. In individual shares, Wartsila traded up 2.2% as it inaugurated a new engine plant in China. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ENERGY: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil futures have recovered slightly in Asian trade after an overnight slump, with Brent only slightly above $100 a barrel.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nymex WTI crude's underperformance is most surprising considering positive economic data and expectations of further inventory tightening, ANZ noted. That said, the post-U.S. Labor day period tends to be weaker as participants start to factor refinery interchanges ahead of the shoulder season, or the period between peak and off-peak seasons, it said. The U.S. EIA said record U.S. crude production drove exports to almost 400,000 bbl/day in June, an increase of 110,000 bbl/day from prior months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nyemx crude was up 35 cents at $93.23/bbl, Brent crude was up 23 cents at $100.57/bbl. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEWS ROUNDUP: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DENMARK: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Novo Nordisk A/S\f28 \uc2 \f2  (NVO) is to discontinue its activities within inflammatory disorders after deciding to increase efforts within diabetes prevention and treatment, obesity and diabetes complications, it said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sandvik\f28 \uc2 \f2 's (SAND.SK) Materials Technology unit has sold its distribution business in Australia and New Zealand to steel distributor Vulcan Steel for an undisclosed price, it said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: Swedish construction company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skanska AB\f28 \uc2 \f2  (SKA-B.SK) has sold the remaining part of the Entre Lindhagen office project in Stockholm, Sweden, to Alecta for about SEK1.7 billion, it said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FINLAND: IndoorAtlas says China's leading search engine \f28 \uc2 \f2 Baidu Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has invested $10 million in the Finnish software developer, whose indoor mapping platform can help retailers track their customers' movements inside buildings.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NORWAY: U.S. regulators on Tuesday deferred a final decision on a controversial effort by European discount airline \f28 \uc2 \f2 Norwegian Air Shuttle\f28 \uc2 \f2  ASA to establish a new long-haul \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Ireland. "The Department continues to review the extensive record and deliberate on the application for longer-term operating authority," DoT said in a statement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DENMARK: The U.S. Federal Maritime Commission is unlikely to approve a proposed alliance between container-shipping giants \f28 \uc2 \f2 Maersk Line\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mediterranean Shipping Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . before consulting with Chinese regulators, according to one of the agency's commissioners.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Christina Zander at christina.zander@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3 Sep 2014 22:54 ET \par Nordic Morning Briefing: Sweden's Riksbank, ECB in Focus\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Jens Hansegard \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR - All times GMT \par Nordic Macro \par  \par 0600 Finland GDP 2Q \par 0730 Sweden Riksbank Rate decision \par  \par Other Macro \par  \par 1145 ECB Rate announcement \par 1215 U.S. \f28 \uc2 \f2 ADP\f28 \uc2 \f2  Jobs Report \par 1400 U.S. ISM non-manufacturing \par  \par Nordic Equities \par  \par 0830 Lego A/S Earnings \par  \par  \par IN FOCUS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Thursday, Sweden's Riksbank will present its rate decision at 0730 GMT. Analysts expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep its rate on hold but to provide for the possibility of lower rates if inflation fails to accelerate during autumn.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Later in the day, attention will turn to the ECB to learn about \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mario Draghi\f28 \uc2 \f2 's plans for the eurozone after the bank's monthly monetary policy meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Locally, investors will digest the outcome of U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barack Obama\f28 \uc2 \f2 's visit to Estonia. In a speech in Tallinn, President Obama pledged \f28 \uc2 \f2 NATO\f28 \uc2 \f2  would defend its Baltic allies and called for a united stand against Russia's aggression, laying blame for the escalating clashes in Ukraine squarely on Moscow.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the corporate from locally, Danish Lego, the world's second biggest toymaker, will present half-year earnings at 0830 GMT. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par  \par EUR/NOK \par Latest 0150 GMT 8.1729-814 \par Previous 2150 GMT 8.1725-801 \par %Chg +0.01 \par  \par EUR/SEK \par Latest 0150 GMT 9.2093-172 \par Previous 2150 GMT 9.2051-134 \par %Chg +0.04 \par  \par USD/NOK \par Latest 0150 GMT 6.2180-236 \par Previous 2150 GMT 6.2154-99 \par %Chg +0.05 \par  \par USD/SEK \par Latest 0150 GMT 7.0064-114 \par Previous 2150 GMT 7.0005-59 \par %Chg -0.02 \par  \par  \par NORDIC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors will closely watch Sweden's Riksbank early Thursday. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to keep its main interest rate on hold at 0.25% at its meeting, according to analysts polled by The Wall Street Journal, but to leave the door open for lower rates if inflation fails to accelerate during autumn.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts at SEB bank said they expect the Riksbank to say it now foresees a rate rise in the first quarter of 2016 compared with expectations in July for an increase in the fourth quarter of next year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Riksbank's forecasts are likely to continue to signal a chance of easing later this year and SEB expects to see a rate cut to 0.15% in October. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STOCK INDEXES: \par  \par OMXN40  1355.25   +8.27  +0.6% \par OMXS30  1398.48  +10.54  +0.8% \par OBX      565.05   +2.62  +0.5% \par OMXC20   743.03   +4.82  +0.7% \par OMXH25  2976.71  +24.64  +0.8% \par  \par Brent   $102.27  -$0.50  -0.5% \par  \par NORDIC MARKETS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nordic markets closed Wednesday's session higher, on reports of a ceasefire deal in eastern Ukraine and amid speculation about a new round of monetary stimulus from the ECB on Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In individual shares, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Carlsberg\f28 \uc2 \f2  and SCA were big gainers, both ending 2.3% higher. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ENERGY: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil futures were slightly lower in Asian trade, retracing after overnight gains.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "WTI shared the Brent market's relief that a ceasefire in Ukraine might be possible, but may have also drawn some support from expectations that U.S. crude oil inventories declined by a million barrels or so in the week ended August 29," analyst Tim Evans at Citi Futures said. Late Wednesday, the API said weekly U.S. stockpiles fell by 545,000 barrels. The inventory data from the U.S. EIA is due later Thursday and analysts expect a drop of 1.1 million barrels.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nymex crude was down 37 cents at $95.17/bbl, Brent crude was down 50 cents at $102.27/bbl. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEWS ROUNDUP: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FINLAND: Finnish paper maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 UPM-Kymmene Oyj\f28 \uc2 \f2  (UPM1V.HE) said Wednesday it has signed a three year outsourcing agreement with Tieto for its selected application management services, with the option of two further years.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: Swedish engineering group \f28 \uc2 \f2 Atlas Copco\f28 \uc2 \f2  (ATCO-A.SK) said it has acquired the compressor distribution and service business from New Zealand's Lancaster Group for an undisclosed sum.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: Swedish defense company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Saab AB (SAAB-B.SK) \f28 \uc2 \f2 announced the creation of a new business unit, as well as personnel changes, that will take effect from 1 January 2015.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FINLAND: Finnish paper maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Stora Enso Oyj\f28 \uc2 \f2  (STERV.HE) said late Tuesday that following its recent acquisition of U.S.-based biotechnology company Virdia, it is investing EUR32 million in a demonstration and market development plant to be built at Raceland, Louisiana, U.S.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Write to Jens Hansegard at jens.hansegard@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 03, 2014 22:54 ET (02:54 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140901ea9100085\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
