\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Markets Morning Read: Russia Stocks Capped -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dimitra DeFotis   \par \uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2014\par 15:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Nearly 300 Russian trucks headed for eastern Ukraine on Tuesday, but Kiev said it won't allow army trucks to enter without Red Cross supervision.\par \par \uc2 The fighting between government troops and pro-Russian separatist militants in eastern \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  has heightened the urgent need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , ABC reports. A Washington Post opinion piece urges Westerners to " Oppose Russia's humanitarian invasion of Ukraine." Major U.S. indexers are putting a lid on inclusion of certain Russian stocks in light of new sanctions.\par \par \uc2 The result: Market Vectors Russia ETF ( RSX) is off by 0.6% in regular trading this morning. The \uc2 iShares MSCI Russia Capped ETF\uc2  (ERUS) declined nearly 1%. For short-term traders, the Direxion Daily Russia Bear 3X Shares ( RUSS) is up nearly 2% after jumping higher in premarket trading, while the Direxion Daily Russia Bull 3X Shares ( RUSL) was down 2%.\par \par \uc2 As German utility EON ( EOAN) preps earnings, emerging market growth in Russia and elsewhere is proving a disappointment, reports Bloomberg's Tino Andreson. Ditto for other utilities. Andreson writes:\par \par \uc2 "EON reports first-half earnings [Wednesday] and ventures in Brazil, Turkey and Russia are expected to contribute to a 24 percent drop in profit from last year, according to analysts ... In Brazil, investments earmarked for utility Eneva (ENEV3) have risen almost fourfold as the business of billionaire partner Eike Batista collapsed. Earnings at Turkish venture \uc2 Haci Omer Sabanci Holding\uc2  (SAHOL) have been held back by a weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and Russia's economy is slowing because of the Ukraine crisis."\par \par \uc2 No big economic news from emerging markets this week. Thursday is the biggest news day on the docket, according to the Reuters calendar: The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2  holds monetary policy meeting and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Uganda\uc2  announces a monetary policy statement. Next week: \uc2 National Bank of Poland\uc2  holds a monetary policy meeting, but an interest rate announcement is not expected Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Barron's Emerging Markets blog, \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 12, 2014 09:48 ET (13:48 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140812ea8c001x4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
