\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russian assets surge after Putin renounces right to invade Ukraine\b0\par\par\uc2 495 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2014\par 15:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * RTS crosses 1,400 points for first time since mid-January\par \par \uc2 * Rouble at multi-month high against euro, dollar (Recasts to reflect new highs, adds comment)\par \par \uc2 By Alexander Winning\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, June 24 (Reuters) - Russian shares and the rouble hit multi-month highs on Tuesday after President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  asked the upper house of Russia's parliament to revoke the right it had granted him to order a military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index was up 2.4 percent at 1,402 points at 1220 GMT, touching its highest since mid-January. The rouble-based MICEX rose 1.3 percent to 1,505 points, reaching levels last seen in mid-February.\par \par \uc2 The rouble strengthened by 1 percent against the dollar to 33.78. It had earlier reached its strongest since January, getting an extra boost from companies converting foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into roubles before they make monthly tax payments.\par \par \uc2 "(Putin's) move will calm down Western/Ukraine hawks constantly calling for a threat of Russian invasion," Dmitry Polevoy, the chief economist for Russia and CIS at \uc2 ING Bank\uc2  in Moscow, wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 "Even though it is difficult to say whether it was a reaction to the remaining threat of extra sanctions ... or simply a strategic play of Mr Putin, it further reduces the probability of tail-risk scenarios in the Ukraine crisis."\par \par \uc2 On March 1, Russian lawmakers granted Putin the right to use the country's army in Ukraine. Their move drew threats of economic sanctions from the West and prompted a selloff in the rouble and Russian assets.\par \par \uc2 Equities have since recouped their losses, after Western sanctions turned out to be weaker than were first feared. But the conflict with Ukraine still exerts a powerful influence over the direction of Russia's stock market.\par \par \uc2 Shares were also supported on Tuesday by reports that pro-Russian separatist leaders in Ukraine's east had agreed to observe a ceasefire with Ukrainian forces, enabling peace talks to proceed.\par \par \uc2 The rouble firmed by 0.83 percent against the euro to reach 46.02 and also touched a five-month high earlier. Besides the softening stance on Ukraine, Russian exporters are converting foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into roubles to pay a mineral extraction tax on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 0.92 percent firmer at 39.29 against the rouble-dollar basket the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses to guide the rouble's nominal exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 In corporate news, U.S. healthcare company \uc2 Abbott Laboratories\uc2  said it had agreed to buy Russian drugmaker \uc2 Veropharm\uc2  in a deal valued at up to $495 million.\par \par \uc2 Veropharm\uc2 's shares were up 35 percent on Monday's close in afternoon trading.\par \par \uc2 For rouble poll data see\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see\par \par \uc2 Russia in graphics: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/dun63s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/dun63s}}}\uc2  (Reporting by Alexander Winning and Jason Bush; Editing by Larry King) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-6-24T14:00:04.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140624ea6o003df\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
