\par\par \b \uc2 Putin Seeks to Defuse Tensions Ahead of EU Leaders Meet -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,258 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2014\par 13:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1100 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--Vladimir Putin's move to have his authority to use military force in Ukraine rescinded sends a signal that Moscow wants to be seen as helping to defuse the pro-Russia insurgency there ahead of a meeting on Friday by EU leaders who have said they are mulling further sanctions against Russia. Coupled with Monday's decision by the rebels to join a cease fire -- which a Kremlin ally played a key role in brokering -- the push to pressure Moscow further could lessen. The invasion of Crimea and the subsequent threat of possible military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in eastern \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  dramatically escalated tensions in the region and led to several rounds of sanctions from the West. While the sanctions were limited, they served as a chilling effect on Russia's economy. But Moscow's markets and the ruble have largely returned to pre-crisis levels, buoyed by Moscow's moves and an apparent reluctance by Europe to impose tougher sanctions. (lukas.albert@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1056 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] India's policy responses to macroeconomic problems will be important in determining foreign direct investment in the short to medium run, \uc2 United Nations Conference on Trade and Development\uc2  says. Inflation and other macroeconomic problems have cast doubt on FDI prospects despite the government's goal to boost it, it says in a report on Tuesday. India is the dominant recipient of FDI in south Asia at $28 billion in 2013. \uc2 Unctad\uc2  says foreign investors are concerned about slowing economic growth, a vulnerable current-account deficit situation and rupee depreciation. (prasanta.sahu@wsj.com, \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @pksahu9)\par \par \uc2 1037 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The outlook for AUD/USD improved on the break above 0.9440 says the UK clearer, who now looks for a revisit of the 2014 highs near 0.9460 and slightly longer-term, the November 7 high of 0.9525. Trading at 0.9400, \uc2 Barclays\uc2  says it would prefer to buy dips while the rate holds above support at 0.9350. (gary.stride@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1022 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--The Turkish lira has absorbed well the rising geopolitical risk so far, says Ishitaa Sharma at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 , and is now trading around 2.13 vs the dollar. "TRY-risk will remain 'an interesting value proposition' in a world of collapsing financial market vols," Citi says. In other words, despite tensions in Iraq investors have not disregarded short-term plays in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At 1100 GMT \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to announce a 50 basis point cut in the trading corridor for the corridor, Citi adds. "The CBT will cut, no doubt about it. What we question here is the speed and the magnitude of the easing." (chiara.albanese@wsj.com @chiaraalbanese)\par \par \uc2 1021 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Standard Bank has held a neutral view on EUR/NOK since early May, but with its indicators turning bullish Tuesday it opens a long position at the current 8.3050 rate, targeting 8.3910 with a stop loss down at 8.1940. (gary.stride@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1020 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Spain's housing bust is not likely to give way to yet another Spanish housing boom, says Fernando Rodriguez, head of the RR de Acuna consultancy and prominent property bear. For starters, Mr. Rodriguez says average prices should fall by an annual 5% through 2017, with only Madrid and some beach locations including Malaga seeing any kind of price increases. On a longer view, Mr. Rodriguez says worsening demographics and a huge stock of built units indicate that Spain's property market may end up resembling Japan's, unless a stronger-than-expected economic recovery \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (david.roman@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1006 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  says that though history suggests that the India budget's influence on short-term performance is declining, market expectations are still important in deciding what the market does after the budget. "If the pre-budget returns are positive, there is a 90% chance that the post-budget returns are negative," the investment bank cautioned. Indian shares are up 1% after the budget's date was announced as July 10. It went up as much as 1.5% earlier in the day. The upcoming budget could be important because of where India is placed cyclically and this is the first non-Congress government in a decade, the bank added. It believes the budget will be positive for cement, financials, metals and mining, oil and gas, property, telecom and utilities. (kenan.machado@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1004 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] If the aim of members of the BOE's rate-setting group was to row back from previous expectations of an interest rate increase before the end of the year, their message seems to have worked somewhat. Sonia rates are now fully pricing in a 25bps rate rise from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  only in January next year, compared with last week's pricing of a rate increase in November this year. (neelabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1002 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Germany's Ifo slump in the business expectations sub-index in June to the lowest level since October doesn't bode well for German exports, says Allianz economist Rolf Schneider. He warns that exports will suffer as long as economic uncertainty amid geopolitical tension in several regions lasts. While this is only a "dent to sentiment in the industry," the high number of recent, less optimistic, business surveys dampens hopes that the German economy could grow substantially above 2% this year, Mr. Schneider says. (ulrike.dauer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0959 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The USD/PHP is higher late Tuesday helped by improvement in U.S. existing home sales. The pair is at 43.86 after closing 43.795 on Monday. "The U.S. housing numbers have trumped the good manufacturing data from China--at least in this market," a local bank trader says. Volume remains moderate. Traders expect the USD/PHP to keep hugging the 43.50-44.00 range in the near term. (cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0956 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Coming up are rate decisions from Turkey (1100 GMT) and Hungary (1200 GMT). \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  is looking for a 50 bps cut to 9% for the key policy rate from Turkey, while it says the \uc2 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should continue its policy of baby-step cuts, with a 10 bps reduction taking the main rate down to 2.3%. (gary.stride@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0955 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--A strong recovery of the ruble versus the dollar poses downside risks to Russia's economic growth, says Bank of America/Merrill Lynch. The ruble hit its strongest level against the dollar since January 23, amid a tentative ceasefire in the Ukraine, combined with an overly hawkish \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. Previously, a weaker ruble and restrictions on imports from Ukraine had helped Russia's economy perform better than expected in the past few months, supported by those industrial sectors most sensitive to exchange rate fluctuations. The bank says risks to growth include the difficult-to-predict developments of the crisis in Ukraine and the fast recovery of the ruble. However, the bank expects the ruble to weaken in late 3Q, which would keep the exchange rate to the dollar at 35.5 for the whole year. (Alexander.Kolyandr@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 24, 2014 07:00 ET (11:00 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140624ea6o0017h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw174\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2610\pichgoal600
