\par\par \b \uc2 Ruble Falls Out of Favor with Russians -- WSJ Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh \par \uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2014\par 18:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Watching the ruble's drop to record lows amid fears of international sanctions against Moscow, Russians rushed to ditch their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and buy foreign money in March in a similar manner as during the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Following an escalation of tensions after Russia's annexation of Crimea and Moscow's warning that it might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  militarily in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect pro-Russians there--moves that caused the ruble to tumble to an all-time low against the dollar and the euro--Russian household demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  peaked in March at a more than five-year high of $14.3 billion in U.S. dollar equivalent terms.\par \par \uc2 In February, households' demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  reached $9.6 billion.\par \par \uc2 The Bank Of Russia in its monthly overview of the domestic foreign cash market said demand for dollars rose 48% in March compared with the prior month, while interest in buying euros rose 50%.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the rise in overall demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March was mostly caused by an intensified cash withdrawal from accounts, which jumped 82% compared with February.\par \par \uc2 This might have been a consequence of international sanctions introduced because of the annexation of Crimea, which targeted \uc2 Bank Rossiya\uc2 --a organization that the \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2  described as the personal lender of senior Russian officials. As a result, both \uc2 Visa Inc\uc2 . and \uc2 MasterCard Inc\uc2 . have stopped servicing the bank, raising concerns that other banks could be similarly affected.\par \par \uc2 Also, an intensified purge of lenders across the country--in the past year alone the Bank of Russia has shut more than 100 banks--has added to households' mistrust of the banking system.\par \par \uc2 The flight to foreign cash reflects a deterioration in the economy that started at the beginning of this year, \uc2 Alfa Bank\uc2  said in a note. Russia bled more than $60 billion in net capital outflows in the first quarter alone, more than during the whole of 2013. The economy ministry said gross domestic product may contract by more than 1% this year should capital flight remain at levels seen in the first three months of this year.\par \par \uc2 The grey cloud of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's data may have a silver lining for the ruble, however.\par \par \uc2 VTB Capital said in a research note that the bank's data confirms a view that high public demand for cash dollars and euros, one of the major drivers for the ruble's depreciation in March, is unlikely to be repeated in the coming months. This could reduce the demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the tourist season, providing some support for the ruble over the summer.\par \par \uc2 The three waves of sanctions imposed by the Western nations against Moscow have so far been less harsh than initially expected, which together with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have helped the ruble to pare some losses since the first trading day of March, when it fell to 37 rubles per dollar. On Monday, the ruble traded at 35.06 against the dollar, though this is still 6.3% weaker than in late 2013.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrew Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Wall Street Journal's Emerging Europe blog,  \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/ }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 12, 2014 12:12 ET (16:12 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140512ea5c002zn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
