\par\par \b \uc2 Morning MoneyBeat Europe: Inflation Data Will Dominate, If Ukraine Lets Them -- WSJ Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By David Cottle   \par \uc2 901 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2014\par 08:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Good Morning Europe\par \par \uc2 European stocks managed a late fightback Monday, despite increased worries about the stability of eastern Ukraine. The U.S. cavalry arrived to rally investors in the form some better than expected retail sales and a well-received earnings report from \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That said a rather flat open is expected Tuesday, with Ukraine still front and center and with it the problem of a coherent response to the crisis from the \uc2 European Union\uc2 . Assuming no escalation, however, inflation data are likely to hold the markets' attention early on. Yet another weak consumer price print is expected from the U.K., which, if seen, could well make life tough for sterling as expectations of tighter monetary policy from the Bank of England will recede.\par \par \uc2 Inflation in the U.S. is also expected to have remained low in March, although it might have picked up from February's notable weakness. In any case it's not expected to pose any threat at all to the taper.\par \par \uc2 By David Cottle\par \par \uc2 Market Snapshot: U.S. stocks (Monday close): DJIA up 0.9%, Nasdaq up 0.6%, S&P 500 up 0.8%. Nikkei ends Tuesday up 0.6%. June FTSE now up 0.1%, June S&P up 0.1%. Brent crude now down 38 cents at $108.69. Gold down $7.60 at $1318.90. EUR/USD now at $1.3816, below $1.3821 late Monday in New York. USD/JPY at Yen101.90, just above Yen101.85. Ten-year T-note yields 2.64%, Bund 1.52% and Gilt 2.63%.\par \par \uc2 Watch For: U.K. inflation data (PPI, CPI), Germany's ZEW sentiment indicator, U.S. CPI.\par \par \uc2 What you may have missed from MoneyBeat:\par \par \uc2 London Housing Looking Less Prime for Dollar Buyers: For Londoners, the city's prime central property market looks unfathomable. Stories of broom cupboards selling for hundreds of thousands of pounds are legion.\par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  Finds Second Alleged Fraud: \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  said it has discovered fraud at a second supplier to Mexican oil company \uc2 Petr\u243\'00\'F3leos Mexicanos\uc2 , or \uc2 Pemex\uc2 , less than two months after the bank said it had investigated its dealings with another supplier, Oceanograf\u237\'00\'EDa.\par \par \uc2 Can The ECB Really Drive Down The Euro?: The signals coming from \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymakers are that persistent euro strength is pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  towards pumping more liquidity into the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy.\par \par \uc2 Massive BOJ-Buying Silences JGB Market: On Monday, the newest 10-year Japanese government bond -- the yield on which is used as a benchmark for bank loans and a barometer of trust in government finances -- didn't trade even once.\par \par \uc2 Companies Piled on The Cash in 2013: U.S. corporate cash piles grew to a record amount in 2013, fueled by a red-hot bond market, a modestly improving economy and tax policy that discourages companies from repatriating money stashed overseas, \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  Ratings Services says in a report to be released Monday.\par \par \uc2 From The Wall Street Journal:\par \par \uc2 Obama, Putin Talk as Unrest Roils Eastern Ukraine : The U.S. stepped up efforts to dissuade Russia from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's increasingly unstable east, with President Barack Obama telling President Vladimir Putin Monday that a diplomatic solution to the crisis is still possible even as he warned against further escalation.\par \par \uc2 GE Rethinks the 20-Year CEO : \uc2 Jeff Immelt\uc2  may give up leadership of \uc2 General Electric\uc2  sooner than his expected 20-year tenure, as he and fellow directors re-evaluate the right term for its chief executive, people familiar with GE's thinking said.\par \par \uc2 Investment Bank Still a Problem For Barclays CFO : In recent private meetings with analysts and investors, \uc2 Barclays\uc2 ' new finance chief, \uc2 Tushar Morzaria\uc2 , surprised attendees with a frank admission, according to participants: The British bank doesn't have a credible plan for what to do with its sprawling investment bank.\par \par \uc2 Housing Trouble Grows In China : Evidence is mounting that in dozens of third- and fourth-tier Chinese cities rarely visited by foreigners, overbuilding is out of control and a major property-market slowdown is now under way.\par \par \uc2 Europe's Junk-Debt Market Peaks : Riskier companies are issuing debt at their fastest-ever clip in Europe, and now the market looks set to welcome its biggest offering on record.\par \par \uc2 Diageo\uc2  Seeks Additional United Spirits Shares: U.K. liquor giant \uc2 Diageo\uc2  and its Dutch unit Relay B.V. on Tuesday made a $1.9 billion open offer to buy an additional 26% stake in India's United Spirits from public shareholders.\par \par \uc2 Italian Premier Renzi Names State-Controlled Company Bosses: Italy's new prime minister, Matteo Renzi, Monday named a slate of new bosses at Italy's biggest state-controlled groups, in one of the first tests of his promise to deliver economic change.\par \par \uc2 Roche Sales Hurt by Strong Swiss Franc: Swiss drug maker \uc2 Roche Holding\uc2  reported Tuesday a 1% dip in first-quarter sales, as a strong Swiss franc eroded the value of growing sales of its cancer drugs.\par \par \uc2 Nestle\uc2  Sales Fall, Missing Expectations: \uc2 Nestle\uc2  reported a 5.1% drop in first-quarter sales on Tuesday, the latest evidence of the world's largest food maker's difficulties in Europe and the Americas. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at The Wall Street Journal's MoneyBeat blog, \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/moneybeat/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/moneybeat/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 15, 2014 02:14 ET (06:14 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140415ea4f000ma\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
