\par\par \b \uc2 European Midday Briefing: European Stocks Hit By Global Sell-Off\b0\par\par\uc2 1,173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2014\par 12:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AMERICAN MARKETS OUTLOOK: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite a slump in European and Asian markets Friday, U.S. futures were largely flat, with investors looking at results from \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wells Fargo\f28 \uc2 \f2  for further direction. The banks are the first among the sector to announce results this earnings season and their numbers tend to be indicative of what to expect from their peers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 "If bloated valuations are indeed an issue then \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2 's results will be of particular interest to investors when they are released later in the session," said Joao Monteiro, analyst at Valutrades.\par \par \uc2 "There remains big questions as to exactly what is driving the current market turbulence: is it the threat of interest rises? Over-heated valuations? One thing is for sure we can expect more turbulence in the coming days."\par \par \uc2 At 1000 GMT, Dow Jones Industrial Average futures were flat at 16105.0 while Nasdaq 100 futures were down 0.1% at 3476.30 and S&P 500 futures were flat at 1827.00. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN MARKETS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European shares came under heavy selling pressure Friday as the global stock market rout continued following sharp falls on Wall Street and then Asia.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As it becomes ever clearer that the Federal Reserve is pretty much fixed in its determination to stop quantitative easing late this year, the oxygen that has fueled the five-year bull market is slowly draining out of the market," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategists Jim Reid and Anthony Ip.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sectors that benefited the most from the easy policy, such as technology and biotech, are the ones that are now suffering, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategists added\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1030 GMT the Euro Stoxx 50 was down 1.2% at 3116.51, while the U.K.'s FTSE 100 was down 1.2% at 6562.82. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was almost unchanged against the yen in Asia due to a lack of fresh trading cues, but traders said the pressure is to the downside, mainly due to selling interest from non-Japanese investors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier, an attempt by speculators to push the dollar down below the technically important Y101.20 line was unsuccessful, one trader said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There was a sense of tension in the market earlier this morning, but we're relieved that we were able to confirm that the support is still strong," said Yuji Saito, executive director of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Agricole\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell to as low as Y101.32, however.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Looking ahead, strategists will pay attention to U.S. data later in the day, including the \f28 \uc2 \f2 University of Michigan\f28 \uc2 \f2  survey of consumers due at 1355 GMT. Economists polled by the Wall Street Journal expect the headline index to rise to 81 in April from 79.9 a month earlier.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Praevidentia Strategy chief strategist Masafumi Yamamoto said another important technical level is Y101.76. If this is breached, the market will become bearish and further downsides may be possible, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 0950 GMT, USD/JPY was at 101.75-78, EUR/USD was at 1.3885-88 and GBP/USD was at 1.6764-66. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =========================== \par TOP STORIES: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IEA Trims 2014 Oil Demand Growth\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The agency highlighted ongoing "elevated" risks in the oil market, as it trimmed its forecast for an increase in demand this year following Russia's annexation of Crimea, but also warned of lower oil production.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ups Portugal Outlook to Positive\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fitch raised its outlook for Portugal to "positive" from "negative," citing the bailed-out euro-zone nation's strong economic recovery and falling budget deficit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 S&P Lowers Finland Outlook\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 S&P cut the outlook on Finland's credit rating to negative from stable because of the Nordic country's continuing economic problems.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sony\f28 \uc2 \f2  Warns on Vaio Battery Fire Risk\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sony\f28 \uc2 \f2  said there was a risk that batteries made by Panasonic in nearly 26,000 of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sony\f28 \uc2 \f2 's newest Vaio personal computers could overheat and catch fire. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =========================== \par  \par INSIGHT & ANALYSIS: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HEARD ON THE STREET: China Stock Markets Grow Closer Together\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Imagine if Americans were barred from investing in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Facebook\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Verizon and \f28 \uc2 \f2 IBM\f28 \uc2 \f2 , and had to smuggle money into Canada to buy their shares. That has effectively been the situation for Chinese investors, writes Aaron Back.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ANALYSIS: Nickel Surge Squeezes Smelters\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A jump in nickel prices this year is increasing the cost of producing nickel pig iron--raising the possibility of a cut in production of this key stainless-steel ingredient in China, the world's dominant producer.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 THE WALL STREET JOURNAL: Markets Hit By Tech Selloff\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors unloaded shares of once-highflying biotechnology and Internet companies over concerns that they are overvalued, pushing the Nasdaq to its worst daily decline since 2011, writes E.S. Browning \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =========================== \par STILL TO COME \par GMT   COUNTRY/PERIOD \par 1230 US  Mar PPI \par 1355 US  Apr Thomson Reuters/ \par              \f28 \uc2 \f2 University of Michigan\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par              Survey of Consumers \par              Sentiment Index \par 1700 US      George Osborne speaks on \par              the economic recovery \par              at U.S. think tank \par 1800 CAN     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2  Weekly \par              Financial Statistics \par N/A  JPN Apr Monthly Economic Report \par N/A  US      IMF and \f28 \uc2 \f2 World Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par              Spring meetings open \par N/A  US      G20 Finance Ministers \par              and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par              Governors Meeting \par              concludes \par  \par =========================== \par  \par OTHER NEWS: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German Inflation Rate Falls Below 1%\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German inflation hit multiyear lows in March. In European harmonized terms, prices increased 0.3% on the month in March, but rose only 0.9% in annual terms, marking the first time it has fallen below 1% since June 2010.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 West Divided in Bid To Curb Russia Over Crimea\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance ministers from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Group of Seven\f28 \uc2 \f2  leading industrialized countries on Thursday considered escalating sanctions against Russia for its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ukraine\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but concerns about potential damage to the European and global economies undermined their efforts to forge a united front.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Sales Rise\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Europe's largest auto maker delivered 7.6% more vehicles across the group in March than a year earlier, helped by Western Europe returning to growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bang & Olufsen Hit On Capital Raising Plan\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares in Danish high-end consumer electronics company dropped 20% after the company announced its it's looking to strengthen its capital base to boost growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some BOJ Board Members Cautious\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a sign that not every \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  policy maker is as upbeat as Gov. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Haruhiko Kuroda\f28 \uc2 \f2  about growth prospects, some of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's board members voiced concerns at last month's meeting over two increasingly crucial parts of the economy: exports and capital investment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan Notes Sales Tax Effect on Retail Sales\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister said that the effect of the recent sales tax increase has been felt widely across the retail sector.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia, China Pursue Expanded \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Trade\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China and Australia's central banks are examining ways to enhance joint clearing and settlement \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as they look to further strengthen direct trading between the Australian dollar and the renminbi, a year after it first became possible. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Simon Varcoe at simon.varcoe@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 11, 2014 06:47 ET (10:47 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140411ea4b0016s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
