\par\par \b \uc2 *\uc2 Czech  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Voted Unanimously To Keep Policy Unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 14:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 27 Mar 2014 09:27 ET *\uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees "Slight" Disinflationary Risks\par \par \uc2 27 Mar 2014 09:27 ET *Czech Ctrl Bk to keep Koruna Weak Until At Least Early '15\par \par \uc2 27 Mar 2014 09:27 ET *Czech Singer: If More Easing Needed, Bk Will Extend Weak Koruna Policy\par \par \uc2 27 Mar 2014 09:27 ET *Czech Singer: Hard to See any Concrete Econ Impact from \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  Crisis\par \par \uc2 27 Mar 2014 09:27 ET *Czech Singer: \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Prevented Fall Into Deflation\par \par \uc2 27 Mar 2014 09:28 ET *Czech Singer: Current Policy Provides Necessary Easing\par \par \uc2 27 Mar 2014 09:28 ET *Czech Singer: Wage Growth in Commercial Sector Muted\par \par \uc2 27 Mar 2014 09:28 ET *Czech Singer: Market Rates to Stay Flat at Low Levels into 2015\par \par \uc2 27 Mar 2014 09:52 ET  \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Unanimous in Maintaining Loose Monetary Conditions\par \par \uc2 By Sean Carney\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE--The \uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees slight disinflationary risks and voted unanimously Thursday to keep interest rates unchanged and to keep its weak-koruna policy in place until "at least" early 2015, Gov. Miroslav Singer said.\par \par \uc2 "The November decision of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  [to launch \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] has prevented a fall into deflation," Mr. Singer said at a briefing after the decision.\par \par \uc2 "This delivers--in the board's view--the necessary easing of monetary conditions," Mr. Singer said.\par \par \uc2 He said that risks to the economy are "slightly on the downside," but aren't strong enough to warrant more easing.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Singer said he expects market interest rates to remain flat at current low levels until the start of next year.\par \par \uc2 If additional monetary easing is needed next year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will extend its weak-koruna policy for a longer period, he said.\par \par \uc2 When asked whether the domestic economy faces any risks from the crisis in Ukraine, Mr. Singer said the monetary policy board discussed this issue, but couldn't see any tangible impact.\par \par \uc2 The country's annual inflation rate has been slowing due to slack consumer demand, a lack of wage growth, and recent energy, telecommunications and utility price cuts, he said.\par \par \uc2 In both January and February, annual inflation was 0.2%, well below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2% target.\par \par \uc2 Recent economic indicators show, however, that the country's economy is recovering, Mr. Singer said. For most of 2012 and 2013, the Czech Republic was in its longest recession in the country's modern history.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark interest rate has been at an historic low of 0.05% since November 2012 and the weak-koruna policy--keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 27.0 to the euro or at weaker levels--has been in place since November of last year.\par \par \uc2 Write to Sean Carney at sean.carney@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 27, 2014 09:52 ET (13:52 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140327ea3r0022y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
