\par\par \b \uc2 CEE Morning Briefing: Hungary Rate Move, Slovakia's ECB Rate Setter in Focus\b0\par\par\uc2 By Leos Rousek   \par \uc2 649 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 03:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   TODAY'S CALENDAR \par   Local/GMT \par   1300/1200 ECB's Makuch at Bratislava conference \par   1400/1300 Hungary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate decision \par   1500/1400 Hungary rate statement \par   1500/1400 Hungary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  latest CPI, GDP forecasts \par     N/A     Czech lawmakers to vote on boosting \par             defense spending \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A likely cut in Hungary's benchmark interest rate to a new record low and comments from Slovakia's policy maker on the Governing Council of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be in focus Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Magyar Nemzeti Bank\uc2  is expected to cut interest rates for the 20th consecutive time to boost fragile economic growth. \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is forecast to cut its main rate 0.1 percentage point to 2.60%, according to 15 of 18 economists polled by The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 The MNB is also due to release its latest forecasts for inflation and economic growth.\par \par \uc2 "Despite the euro-forint rising above 313 several times since the beginning of March, [governing party] Fidesz's polling numbers do not seem affected by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness," said \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  economist Dan Bucsa in a note to clients Monday, referring to parliamentary elections in April.\par \par \uc2 Also Tuesday, Jozef Makuch, an ECB interest rate setter, is likely to comment on possible measures the ECB could take to help the euro area's economic recovery, after it cut its headline interest rate by half in November to 0.25%.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Makuch, who is also governor of the National Bank of Slovakia, will speak at a conference to present the bank's latest economic growth and inflation outlook for this small euro-area country of 5 million people.\par \par \uc2 Unlike other countries that share the euro, Slovakia has avoided falling into recession since 2009 following the onset of the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 In Prague, Czech lawmakers are scheduled to vote on a bill sponsored by legislators behind the ruling coalition government to boost the country's defense spending to 1.3% of gross domestic product as of 2015, from 1.08% now. The motion to raise defense spending reflects the country's heightened security concerns in the wake of events in Ukraine and Crimea, the lawmakers behind the bill say. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par EUR/CZK \par Latest 0250 GMT 27.382-452 \par Previous 2150 GMT 27.409-46 \par %Chg -0.04 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par Latest 0250 GMT 312.78-3.78 \par Previous 2150 GMT 312.92-3.47 \par % Chg +0.03 \par  \par EUR/PLN \par Latest 0250 GMT 4.1958-2058 \par Previous 2150 GMT 4.1975-2040 \par % Chg +0.00 \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par Hungary \par          Mon    Fri \par 3 yrs   4.69%  4.66% \par 5 yrs   5.01%  4.98% \par 10yrs   5.82%  5.77% \par  \par  \par Poland \par           Mon    Fri \par 3 yrs    3.07%  2.95% \par 5 yrs    3.56%  3.61% \par 10yrs    4.24%  4.29% \par  \par  \par Czech Republic \par           Mon    Fri \par 3 yrs    0.60%  0.61% \par 5 yrs    1.11%  1.11% \par 10yrs    2.20%  2.20% \par  \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG 20 \par 2,361.78-4.18-0.18% \par  \par BUX \par 16,825.50+65.51+0.39% \par  \par PX \par 990.37-1.17-0.12% \par  \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UKRAINE: Leaders of the world's largest economies agreed Monday to effectively remove Russia from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Group of Eight\f28 \uc2 \f2  nations in response to Moscow's military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ukraine\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The leaders meeting in The Hague also sharpened their warnings against Russia over the crisis in Ukraine, threatening "significant consequences" for annexing Crimea and pledging broader economic sanctions should Moscow continue to pressure Ukraine.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Margit Feher in Budapest contributed to this article.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Leos Rousek at leos.rousek@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope}}}\uc2 \f2  for the new WSJ and Dow Jones blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 24, 2014 22:57 ET (02:57 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140325ea3p000bm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
