\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Russian stocks track emerging equities higher, rouble back in red\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sujata Rao   \par \uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 11:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 18 (Reuters) - Russia's rouble fell on Tuesday from the previous session's two-week highs on fears of fresh economic sanctions and a further military standoff, though Moscow equities firmed in line with other emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Equities were generally stronger across emerging markets, lifted by big gains in Indian and Korea, while Russian shares extended the 3.6 percent rise posted on Monday after Western sanctions were seen as milder than expected.\par \par \uc2 But Moscow's defiant move towards formally annexing the Crimea region is keeping alive tensions with the West. President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is expected to back absorbing the territory into Russia when he addresses parliament later in the day.\par \par \uc2 HSBC\uc2  strategist Murat Toprak said investors would scan Putin's speech for clues as to whether military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely for the rest of \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The rouble weakened 0.6 percent against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The Crimea election is a done deal, the market wants to know if there is any intention to go beyond Crimea. This is one of the concerns of the market," Toprak said.\par \par \uc2 Fears the West will respond with fresh, more stringent sanctions are reflected in the offshore rouble forwards, which continue to trade at a rare premium to onshore contracts on fears that future local settlements could prove difficult.\par \par \uc2 In neighbouring Ukraine, the hryvnia fell more than 4 percent to the dollar. Investors are waiting to see the result of an IMF mission to Kiev which concludes on Friday. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility is one of the IMF's demands.\par \par \uc2 "What happens to hryvnia depends on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and given the level of their \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves I'd expect that authorities would not stand in the way of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said RBS analyst Tatiana Orlova.\par \par \uc2 "On the basis of fundamentals, hryvnia should move to 11 or 12 per dollar."\par \par \uc2 While broader emerging markets have been boosted by better economic data from many countries, including the so-called Fragile Five, gains were seen capped by Chinese developments.\par \par \uc2 The yuan traded almost at one-year lows to the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weekend move to widen its trading band, indicating it was willing to tolerate more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility. Traders expect more weakness as the economy loses steam.\par \par \uc2 "The China backdrop is not very supportive - all these uncertainties about potential bankruptcies - this is a market concern, it's not very positive for emerging markets," Toprak said, referring to recent corporate difficulties.\par \par \uc2 Chinese stocks ended flat but MSCI's emerging markets index rose 0.2 percent, buoyed by gains in Seoul which posted the biggest one-day rise in two weeks and in Mumbai where foreign buyers pushed shares to record highs before elections.\par \par \uc2 Overseas funds have bought a net $1.6 billion worth of Indian shares in the past 20 sessions, while \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  upped its recommendation on Indian shares to overweight.\par \par \uc2 Turkish equities were a quarter point higher but the lira fell 0.4 percent ahead of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting that is expected to leave interest rates unchanged. The bank jacked up all its interest rates by 250-500 basis points at the end of January to protect the lira.\par \par \uc2 \f2               \par               \par               \par               \par               \par For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par               \par For TURKISH market report, see\par \par               \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For RUSSIAN market report, see )\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-3-21T10:51:45.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140318ea3i00bym\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
