\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ.com What's News - Worldwide News Briefs For Mar 18\b0\par\par\uc2 884 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 15:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KARZAI NOMINATES MEMBER OF OPPOSITION AS VICE PRESIDENT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Afghan President Hamid Karzai nominated an opposition Tajik politician as a replacement vice president, a choice that could help bridge differences with the opposition as crucial elections approach. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRANCE POSTPONES PLANS TO ATTEND TALKS IN MOSCOW \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 France postponed plans for a senior delegation to attend talks in Moscow as the West pushed to deepen the Kremlin's isolation on the world stage in the wake of Russia's military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ukraine\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN SUSPENDS RUSSIAN VISA TALKS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Calling Crimea's referendum for independence "unconstitutional" under Ukrainian law, Japan announced Tuesday that it will suspend ongoing talks with Russia on relaxing visas and investment, space cooperation and defense accords. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREECE REACHES DEAL TO UNLOCK AID \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece reached an agreement with a troika of international debt inspectors on the reforms the country must take to receive billions of euros in frozen aid payments dating from the middle of last year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OECD WARNS AGAINST MORE CUTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Governments seeking to further narrow their budget deficits should ensure spending cuts don't reduce support for vulnerable groups and further increase poverty and income inequality, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK OF ENGLAND SHAKES UP TOP TEAM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. treasury made three appointments to the Bank of England's top team and shuffled seats on its two policy committees as part of an unprecedented overhaul of the 320-year-old \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to be unveiled later by Gov. Mark Carney. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AIR CANADA\f28 \uc2 \f2  HALTS VENEZUELA FLIGHTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Air Canada said it has suspended flights to Venezuela, citing security concerns in the wake of antigovernment protests. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA TO APPEAL ITALIAN RULING ON HELICOPTER DEPOSIT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India said it will appeal an Italian court order which rejected its attempts to recover the 278 million euros it had put down for a scrapped helicopter deal with Italian defense contractor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Finmeccanica\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRANCE ARRESTS GREENPEACE PROTESTERS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Several Greenpeace activists were arrested after they broke into the Fessenheim nuclear power plant in eastern France and put up a giant banner demanding the closure of nuclear reactors in Europe. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SWISS TRIM 2014 GROWTH FORECAST \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Swiss government trimmed its economic growth forecast slightly for this year but still expects the global economic recovery to boost its exports. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. FORCES TAKE CONTROL OF LIBYAN TANKER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Navy\f28 \uc2 \f2  commandos seized a tanker loaded with Libyan crude near Cyprus early Monday, thwarting an attempted sale by rebels who defied the weak central government and tried to grab a share of the North African nation's oil wealth. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SERBIA'S VU\u268\'01\'0CI\u262\'01\'06 PLANS 'PAINFUL' MEASURES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Serbia's likely new prime minister said he plans "several painful" steps to narrow the nation's budget deficit after his party won parliamentary elections on Sunday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par QE NOT THE ONLY OPTION FOR ECB ON INFLATION \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Europe File: The solution is a thorough cleanup of the banking system of the sort that the ECB is currently orchestrating. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.K. CONDEMNS RUSSIA'S ACTIONS ON UKRAINE IN STRONGEST TERMS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Britain condemned "in the strongest terms" Russia's actions in Ukraine after President Vladimir Putin defied international pressure and recognized Crimea as an independent state on Monday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PERU'S CONGRESS RATIFIES CABINET \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Peru's Congress voted to ratify President Ollanta Humala's new cabinet after initially refusing to do so, averting a crisis that could have hurt investor confidence and despite the opposition's complaints about the first lady. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CANADA IMPOSES TRAVEL BAN ON RUSSIAN OFFICIALS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canada joined its Western allies Monday in unveiling additional sanctions against Russia in an effort to isolate the country for its role in "undermining" Ukraine's sovereignty. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IRAN TALKS RESUME AMID UKRAINE CRISIS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Iran and six major powers begin on Tuesday a fresh round of high-level nuclear talks, the first since tensions erupted within the six-power group over Ukraine. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VENEZUELAN SECURITY FORCES TAKE OVER ALTAMIRA PLAZA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Government said hundreds of National Guard and police were deployed before dawn to take control of the key site of antigovernment protests. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. WANTS TO BAR TRIAL TESTIMONY BY 9/11 SUSPECT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prosecutors in the terror trial of Osama bin Laden's son-in-law asked a judge to block supporting testimony by alleged 9/11 mastermind Khalid Sheik Mohammed. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MAJOR BRAZIL AIRPORTS BEHIND SCHEDULE FOR WORLD CUP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Three major airports under renovations were behind schedule, according to a report released by Brazil's airport authority, but it isn't worried just yet as it continues to work to help them meet the deadline in time for the World Cup. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WEAK PESO WATERS COLOMBIA'S GARDEN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A 12% drop in the value of Colombia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the dollar in the last year has been a boon to its exports. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RENZI SAYS ITALY WON'T BREACH MAASTRICHT LIMITS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italian Prime Minister Matteo Renzi insisted Monday that Rome has no intention of asking to breach the fiscal rules set down for the euro area in Maastricht more than 20 years ago. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IRAN CONSIDERING EXPORTING LNG VIA PLANT IN OMAN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The move would allow the country greater access to gas-hungry Far-Eastern markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (For continuously updated news from the Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 .)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 18, 2014 10:00 ET (14:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140318ea3i001ug\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
