\par\par \b \uc2 Nordic Morning Briefing: Russia Faces Sanctions After Crimea Vote\b0\par\par\uc2 By Charles Duxbury   \par \uc2 3,501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 04:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR - All times GMT \par  \par Nordic Macro \par   0900 Norway Trade Feb \par  \par Other Macro \par  1000 EU CPI Feb Final \par  1230 U.S Empire Mfg Mar \par  1315 U.S Ind. Prod. Feb \par  \par Nordic Equities \par  0700 \f28 \uc2 \f2 H&M\f28 \uc2 \f2  Sales \par  \par IN FOCUS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 More than 95% of Crimeans voted to break away from Ukraine and rejoin Russia, according to preliminary results, in a referendum that raises the stakes in the most acute East-West confrontation since the Cold War.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The U.S. and \uc2 European Union\uc2  quickly condemned the referendum as illegal. President Barack Obama, speaking by phone with Russian President Vladimir Putin, told him Sunday that the Crimean vote took place "under duress of Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " and wouldn't be recognized. The Russian leader responded that the vote fully complied with international norms, the Kremlin said, issuing a statement that showed no sign of diplomatic progress in the crisis.\par \par \uc2 Russia faces sanctions as early as Monday in its standoff with the West and Ukraine over the Crimea peninsula, Poland's foreign minister told Austrian weekly magazine Profil over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 "We are discussing several options with EU members and the U.S.," Poland's Radoslaw Sikorski was quoted in an interview published on the magazine's website.\par \par \uc2 "We didn't seek confrontation. But if Russia doesn't come around, the EU's foreign ministers will give a first response Monday," Frank-Walter Steinmeier, German foreign minister, was quoted as saying in Welt am Sonntag, a German newspaper.\par \par \uc2 Among regional data, local focus in the Nordics will be on Norwegian trade data for February early in the session before moving to the U.S for manufacturing data later on. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par EUR/NOK \par Latest 0250 GMT 8.3033-118 \par Previous 2150 GMT 8.3002-161 \par %Chg -0.01 \par  \par EUR/SEK \par Latest 0250 GMT 8.8860-942 \par Previous 2150 GMT 8.8776-926 \par %Chg +0.06 \par  \par USD/NOK \par Latest 0250 GMT 5.9708-60 \par Previous 2150 GMT 5.9691-788 \par %Chg -0.01 \par  \par  \par USD/SEK \par Latest 0250 GMT 6.3898-948 \par Previous 2150 GMT 6.3841-932 \par %Chg +0.06 \par  \par NORDIC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts at Nordea bank said that short term they see a range-bound EUR/SEK, between 8.80 and 9.00.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We find arguments supportive of a slightly stronger SEK and see no obvious reason why the spot should cross 9.00 again," they said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If the sale of the remaining stake of Swedish truck maker Scania to German \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen\f28 \uc2 \f2  goes through, that should support SEK over the coming month, the analysts added. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par STOCK INDEXES: \par  \par OMXN40 1290.80    -14.12      -1.1% \par OMXS30 1326.82    -14.12      -1.1% \par OBX     492.73    -3.22       -0.7% \par OMXC20  681.01    -12.10      -1.8% \par OMXH25 2777.00     +0.51       0.0% \par  \par Brent  $108.35     +0.14      +0.1% \par  \par NORDIC MARKETS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Focus will remain on Ukraine and the Crimea referendum to join Russia, analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danske Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The referendum [was] expected to be in favor of joining Russia, so focus will be on Russia's reaction to the request and how Europe and the U.S. will respond to a possible Russian annexation of Crimea," the analysts said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amid the geopolitical strife in Europe, markets were down Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Focus also on \f28 \uc2 \f2 H&M\f28 \uc2 \f2  sales due 0700 GMT Monday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ENERGY: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil futures were higher in Asia after the Crimea election. Over the weekend, Russian forces had partially pulled back from an incursion into mainland Ukraine. "With the overwhelming pro-Russian vote in the region clashing with the West's assertions that the referendum is not valid, expect further geopolitical risk-related support this week," ANZ said. It also said the El Sharara oilfield in Libya halted production once again, less than a week after returning to production. Overall, speculative holdings remain quite high with plenty of potential for a further cycle of selling, Citi Futures said. Nymex crude was up 24 cents at $99.13/bbl, and Brent crude was up 14 cents at $108.35/bbl.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CME Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said U.S. natural gas futures rallied in Sunday night trading, up 1.9% to $4.51 per mm BTU on the news that Russian forces had seized control of a natural-gas terminal just outside the border of Crimea. Europe is dependent on Russia for 30% of its gas supply. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NEWS ROUNDUP: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FINLAND: India's top court dismissed \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nokia Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s recent appeal of a lower court order related to a continuing tax dispute that has cast a shadow over the Finnish company's $7.5 billion deal to sell its handset business to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Microsoft Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: Scandinavian airline \f28 \uc2 \f2 SAS AB\f28 \uc2 \f2  (SAS.SK) said its net loss narrowed in its fiscal first quarter as cost reductions only partly offset over capacity and low growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DENMARK: Danish jewellery maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pandora A/S\f28 \uc2 \f2  (PNDORA.KO) said shareholders Axcel III K/S 1, Axcel III K/S 2, Axcel III K/S 3, Pewic Holding ApS and Christian Algot Enevoldsen have agreed to sell a total of 13 million existing shares in Pandora in an accelerated bookbuilt offering.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FINLAND: Finnish telecom equipment maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nokia Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (NOK) is planning to appoint Rajeev Suri as its next chief executive, Finnish newspaper Helsingin Sanomat reported on its website citing unnamed Finnish and foreign sources.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Write to Charles Duxbury at charles.duxbury@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 17 Mar 2014 23:12 EDT \par Nordic Morning Briefing: Ukraine Developments in View\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Christina Zander \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR - All times GMT \par  \par Nordic Macro \par  \par  \par Other Macro \par  \par 1000 Euro zone, ZEW Economic Sentiment \par 1000 Germany, ZEW Economic Sentiment \par 1230 U.S, Housing Starts, Feb. \par  \par  \par IN FOCUS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On an otherwise thin agenda, focus will Tuesday remain on the crisis in Ukraine and Russia's reactions to sanctions imposed by the U.S. and the EU Monday. Nordic investors are carefully monitoring their eastern neighbour and any sign that tensions are escalating will have a negative impact on risk appetite.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  Monday slapped an asset freeze and travel ban on 13 Russian and eight Crimean leaders and warned that tougher measures could come by week's end.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The move came a day after Crimeans voted overwhelmingly to leave Ukraine and join Russia in a referendum denounced by Western leaders as illegal and rigged. The vote left the U.S. and Europe on edge over whether Russia would raise the stakes further by annexing Crimea or sending troops into eastern Ukraine.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Wednesday, investors will turn their attention to the U.S and the Fedral Open Market Committee meeting, the first with Janet Yellen as chair for the Federal Reserve. The American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is widely expected continue to reduce its asset purchases by $10 billion. Focus will be on forward guidance as unemployment is declining much faster than the FOMC had previously anticipated. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par EUR/NOK \par Latest 0250 GMT 8.2892-938 \par Previous 2150 GMT 8.2818-91 \par %Chg +0.07 \par  \par EUR/SEK \par Latest 0250 GMT 8.8627-710 \par Previous 2150 GMT 8.8392-477 \par %Chg +0.26 \par  \par USD/NOK \par Latest 0250 GMT 5.9499-524 \par Previous 2150 GMT 5.9492-531 \par %Chg +0.00 \par  \par USD/SEK \par Latest 0250 GMT 6.3615-66 \par Previous 2150 GMT 6.3495-546 \par %Chg +0.19 \par  \par NORDIC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nordic investors will carefully follow the developments in Ukraine Tuesday and Russia's reactions to the sanctions imposed by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Any sign that tensions are escalating is negative for risk sentiment," said Richard Falkenh\u228\'00\'E4ll, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at SEB.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He notes that a significant drop in risk appetite could weaken the Scandinavian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as investors turn to more stable alternatives like the euro or the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Later in the week attention will turn to the U.S and the FOMC meeting, the first with Janet Yellen as chair of the Federal Reserve. The American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is widely expected to continue to reduce its asset purchases by $10 billion and focus will be on forward guidance as the unemployment is declining much faster than FOMC had previously anticipated. Fed has guided for a first rate hike when the unemployment rate hits 5.9% to 6.0%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It will be interesting to see if the bank presents a new target," said Mr. Falkenh\u228\'00\'E4ll. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par STOCK INDEXES: \par  \par OMXN40  1,312.16  +21.36   +1.7% \par OMXS30  1,349.39  +22.57   +1.7% \par OBX       496.94  +4.21    +0.9% \par OMXC20    686.12  +5.11    +0.8% \par OMXH25  2,819.90  +42.90   +1.5% \par  \par Brent  $106.38    +0.14    +0.1% \par  \par NORDIC MARKETS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nordic investors are carefully monitoring Russia's reactions to the sanctions imposed by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  for any sign that tensions are escalating as this will have a negative impact on risk appetite.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nordic markets shrugged off the ongoing tensions Monday, however, and ended the session higher in line with the rest of Europe where benchmark stock index rebounded after its biggest weekly loss since January, as \f28 \uc2 \f2 RWE AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Soci\u233\'00\'E9t\u233\'00\'E9 G\u233\'00\'E9n\u233\'00\'E9rale SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vodafone Group PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose after deal activity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OMXN40 closed up 1.7% at 1,312.16; OBX up 0.9% at 496.94. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vestas Wind Systems\f28 \uc2 \f2  gained 5.1% following an order from German juwi and \f28 \uc2 \f2 H&M\f28 \uc2 \f2  traded up 1.1% as its February sales increased 11% compared with the same month last year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ENERGY: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil futures were mixed in Asia trade as markets look to U.S. oil supply data for cues. Oil prices dropped sharply Monday as Western sanctions on Russia fell short of expectations. "Initial U.S. sanctions were confined to a few select Russian and Ukrainian officials and allayed fears of any major supply disruptions to energy markets. We expect some mild volatility to continue as participants flux on the impact of the Crimean referendum," ANZ said. U.S. weekly oil inventory data from the API were due later today, and the EIA data on Wednesday. ANZ said market expectations are of a further 2.4 million barrel build in U.S. crude stocks and a draw in both gasoline and distillate stocks. Nymex crude was down 18 cents at $97.90/bbl, while Brent crude was up 14 cents at $106.38/bbl. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NEWS ROUNDUP: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: HENNES & MAURITZ AB (HM-B.SK), the Swedish fashion retailer, said Monday its total sales in February, including VAT, increased by 11% in local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  compared with the same month last year. Analysts polled by Dow Jones Newswires had on average expected a 13.8% sales increase in February. Sales including VAT in the first quarter of \f28 \uc2 \f2 H&M\f28 \uc2 \f2 's financial year 2013/2014, i.e. Dec. 1, 2013 to Feb.28, 2014, increased on year by 13%, to SEK37.52 billion from SEK33.15 billion. First-quarter sales excluding VAT increased to SEK32.14 billion from SEK28.39 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DENMARK: VESTAS WIND SYSTEMS A/S (VWS.KO) it and German wind power plant developer juwi signed a framework agreement for 75 units of Vestas' 3 MW platform, with an order for 21 MW now firm and unconditional. The firm order consists of seven V112-3.0 MW turbines to be installed in Rhineland-Palatinate during the third quarter of 2014.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NORWAY: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kodal Minerals PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  (KOD.LN), which has extraction licenses for a phosphate and iron project in southern Norway, said Monday that it has been granted seven new Exploration Permits by the Norwegian Directorate of Mining.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Christina Zander at christina.zander@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 18 Mar 2014 22:59 EDT \par Nordic Morning Briefing: FOMC Meeting In View\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Jens Hansegard \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR - All times GMT \par Nordic Macro \par  \par 0845 Riksbank Governor \par Stefan Ingves Speech \par 0855 Iceland Rate Decision \par  \par Other Macro \par  \par 0930 U.K. BoE Mar. 6 Minutes \par 1230 U.S. Trade Balance 4Q \par 1800 U.S. FOMC Rate Announcement \par  \par Nordic Equities \par  \par N/A  Swedbank AGM \par 0730 Saab Gripen seminar \par  \par  \par Other Equities \par  \par N/A \f28 \uc2 \f2 Inditex\f28 \uc2 \f2  FY 2013 \par  \par IN FOCUS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nordic investors are expected to trade cautiously ahead of Wednesday's big event--the conclusion of the Federal Open Market Committee's two-day meeting, followed by a press conference half an hour later given by Fed Chairwoman Janet Yellen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The FOMC is expected to announce a further cut of 10 billion dollars per month in its bond-buying program.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Anything in the statement that shifts investors away from expecting a continuation of this rate of reduction at each meeting will be jumped on. But despite jitters in stock markets last week and some weather-affected economic data, there's little in the numbers to suggest that the Fed is going to move from that path.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors will also continue to keep an eye on Ukraine and Russia's reactions to sanctions imposed by the U.S. and the EU. Although investors were relieved after Mr. Putin addressed the Russian parliament Tuesday and indicated he had no further designs on Ukraine territories, any signs that tensions are escalating will put a hamper on risk appetite. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par EUR/NOK \par Latest 0250 GMT 8.2856-952 \par Previous 2150 GMT 8.2949-3035 \par %Chg -0.11 \par  \par EUR/SEK \par Latest 0250 GMT 8.8250-338 \par Previous 2150 GMT 8.8164-240 \par %Chg +0.10 \par  \par USD/NOK \par Latest 0250 GMT 5.9497-558 \par Previous 2150 GMT 5.9532-86 \par %Chg -0.05 \par  \par  \par USD/SEK \par Latest 0250 GMT 6.3370-424 \par Previous 2150 GMT 6.3276-323 \par %Chg +0.15 \par  \par NORDIC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With no additional inflation readings ahead of the Riksbank's rate decision on April 9, investors in Nordic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to monitor the developments in Ukraine.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nordea says tensions in the Ukraine have raised the question of what would happen to the SEK in case of sudden risk aversion and sharp equity sell-offs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Historically, these periods have been associated with a weaker krona," Nordea said, noting however that in calmer periods the krona correlates only weakly with equities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Thus, a sharp move lower in stocks would naturally be pushing the krona away from our forecasts," the bank said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par STOCK INDEXES: \par  \par OMXN40  1325.65   +13.49   +1.0% \par OMXS30  1359.07   +9.68    +0.7% \par OBX     499.10    +2.16    +0.4% \par OMXC20  693.48    +7.36    +1.1% \par OMXH25  2844.21   +24.31   +0.9% \par  \par Brent  $106.60    -0.19    -0.2% \par  \par NORDIC MARKETS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the corporate agenda Wednesday, investors in Swedish clothing retailer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hennes & Mauritz\f28 \uc2 \f2  will scrutinize full-year results from Spain's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Inditex\f28 \uc2 \f2 , owner of Zara and the biggest clothing retailer by revenue in the world.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  recently cut \f28 \uc2 \f2 Inditex\f28 \uc2 \f2 's price target to EUR105 from EUR114, in anticipation of a 10% decrease in EPS last year. \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  notes, among other factors, that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Inditex\f28 \uc2 \f2  suffers from rising cost sales ratios, plus potentially an underlying slowdown in demand.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Tuesday, Nordic stocks rose for a second day straight, as concerns over Russia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ukraine\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to ease. Nevertheless, investors will continue to closely watch developments in Ukraine. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ENERGY: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil futures drifted lower in Asia after settling higher Tuesday on reports of the Seaway pipeline expanding capacity by May-June. "U.S. inflation figures, which were broadly in line with expectations and positive housing data, helped WTI close the Brent discount to $7/bbl," ANZ said. "Putin's signing of a treaty to annex Crimea also supported oil markets a little. However, the general consensus is that neither Russia nor Europe can afford to cut energy ties," the bank noted. The closely watched survey from the U.S. EIA is due later Wednesday. U.S. oil inventories are projected to have increased by 2.3 million barrels, on average, in the week ended March 14, according to a Wall Street Journal survey. The API said late Tuesday that its own data for last week showed crude stocks rose by 5.9 million barrels. Nymex crude was down 28 cents at $99.42/bbl, and Brent crude was down 19 cents at $106.60/bbl. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NEWS ROUNDUP: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: An independent committee formed to assess \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's (VOW.XE) bid for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Scania AB\f28 \uc2 \f2  (SCV-A.SK) recommended that Scania shareholders reject the offer.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NORWAY: Norwegian financial advisory and wealth management company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Agasti Holding ASA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (AGA.OS) said that its Navigea Securities AS subsidiary has received a notification from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Financial Supervisory Authority of Norway\f28 \uc2 \f2  regarding planned withdrawal of Navigea's licenses, following the authority's on-site inspection in Apr. 2013.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DENMARK: Danish ship fuel supplier \f28 \uc2 \f2 OW Bunker\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it has set an indicative price range of DKK120 to DKK150 per share for its upcoming IPO, implying a market cap of DKK4.4 billion to DKK5.5 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mojang AB\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the Swedish maker of computer game "Minecraft," boosted profit and revenue sharply last year, underscoring the resilience of the game five years after its debut.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Write to Jens Hansegard at jens.hansegard@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 19 Mar 2014 23:03 EDT \par Nordic Morning Briefing: Ukraine Crisis in Focus\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Charles Duxbury \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR - All times GMT \par Nordic Macro \par  \par 0800 Denmark Retail Sales \par 0830 Sweden Riksbank Account of \par 2013 Policy \par 1730 Riksbank Skingsley Speech \par  \par Other Macro \par  \par 0830 Swiss SNB Rate Decision \par 1500 U.S. Home Sales \par  \par Nordic Equities \par  \par 0730 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volvo AB\f28 \uc2 \f2  Truck Deliveries \par  \par IN FOCUS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The latest developments in Ukraine will remain in sharp focus Thursday as investors seek to interpret the strategies of Russia's president and Ukrainian leaders over the disputed region of Crimea.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Barack Obama on Thursday ruled out a "military excursion" by the United States in Ukraine, saying that engaging Russia militarily "would not be appropriate," NBC News reported.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pro-Russian forces in Crimea stormed Ukraine's naval headquarters and smashed their way into another base with a tractor on Wednesday, Russian and Ukrainian media reported.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Among other events, the Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will make a policy statement and U.S. home sales data are due. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par EUR/NOK \par Latest 0250 GMT 8.3643-702 \par Previous 2150 GMT 8.3458-524 \par %Chg +0.22 \par  \par EUR/SEK \par Latest 0250 GMT 8.8686-772 \par Previous 2150 GMT 8.8528-91 \par %Chg +0.19 \par  \par USD/NOK \par Latest 0250 GMT 6.0496-528 \par Previous 2150 GMT 6.0338-78 \par %Chg +0.26 \par  \par  \par USD/SEK \par Latest 0250 GMT 6.4144-96 \par Previous 2150 GMT 6.4002-42 \par %Chg +0.23 \par  \par  \par NORDIC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts at Handelsbanken see some weakness looming for the Swedish krona. "Continued low inflation will likely remain a burden for the SEK, and we continue to see upside risk to EUR/SEK from here," they said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Buy on dips," they said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Similarly, the analysts say the Norwegian krone remains vulnerable to weak data over the coming period. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STOCK INDEXES: \par  \par OMXN40 1321.17   -4.48     -0.3% \par OMXS30 1360.48   +1.41     +0.1% \par OBX    498.86    -0.24     -0.1% \par OMXC20 690.39    -3.09     -0.5% \par OMXH25 2822.64   -21.57    -0.8% \par  \par Brent  $106.41   +0.29     +0.3% \par  \par NORDIC MARKETS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors will start the session by taking on board the Fed's policy statement due after hours Wednesday - the first for new chairwoman Janet Yellen. She said the Fed could hike rates "something on the order of six months" after the Fed fully winds down its bond-buying program.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Focus early on will also be on Volvo truck deliveries data for February.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Deliveries rose 26% on the year in January, largely due to a strong performance by the group's Volvo brand in North America. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   ENERGY: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil futures were slightly higher in Asia after the U.S. and European oil benchmarks moved in opposite directions Wednesday on mixed cues. Nymex WTI crude was supported by a lower-than-expected increase in U.S. oil stockpiles. "Demand statistics and refinery utilisation rates were also supportive," ANZ said. Brent prices were relatively calm despite the Ukraine crisis, Citi Futures said. Nymex crude was up 13 cents at $100.50/bbl, and Brent crude was up 29 cents at $106.14/bbl. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NEWS ROUNDUP: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: A Swedish man convicted of eight murders will be released from the psychiatric institution where he has been held since the early 1990s, after all murder sentences against him were overturned.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ICELAND: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Iceland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  left interest rates unchanged on Wednesday, backing away from a February forecast that borrowing costs could need to rise in the short term to ease inflationary pressure.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volvo AB\f28 \uc2 \f2  (VOLV-B.SK) Wednesday launched a new range of buses specifically designed for growth markets as it tries to grab market share in emerging economies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWEDEN: \f28 \uc2 \f2 SKF AB\f28 \uc2 \f2  (SKF-B.SK), the Swedish ball bearing maker, said it has reached a EUR315 million settlement with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  following an investigation by the authority regarding an automotive-parts cartel.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Write to Charles Duxbury at charles.duxbury@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 19, 2014 23:03 ET (03:03 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140317ea3h0001s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
